-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  HookABI.pcpp - the HookABI unit: `import HookABI;` hooks C ABI functions.

  Link-time hooks. A hook is a plain routine with C linkage and the hooked
  function's name and C signature, written anywhere in the program:

    routine clink fopen(const APath: ptr to const char;
      const AMode: ptr to const char): ptr to FILE;

  Its definition is in the final link, so it binds every reference to that
  name in the link: the program's own calls and the calls inside C / C++
  libraries linked into it (static archives included). Inside the hook,
  HookReal finds the real function (the definition the hook stands in for,
  see "Finding the real function" below) once, into a slot the hook keeps,
  and the hook calls it through its own routine type (see HookReal's
  example). Code outside the final link (a DLL / .so loaded at run time) is
  the run-time level's job, not this one.

  A header that declares the function noexcept (glibc's __THROW: stat,
  access, ...) needs nothing more: clang takes the exception specification
  from the system header's declaration, the definition compiles clean.

  Windows (COFF) needs two more lines per hooked import. A DLL function is
  reached through an import slot named __imp_<fn>; code compiled against a
  dllimport declaration references that slot, not <fn>. If the link finds
  no __imp_<fn> of the program's own, it pulls the import library member,
  which defines <fn> as well: a duplicate of the hook. So every hooked DLL
  function gets its own slot, right after the hook:

    HOOKABI_IMPORT_SLOT(fopen_s);

  (on Linux the macro expands to nothing that defines a symbol, so it can be
  written on both targets). The mingw headers declare many CRT names
  dllimport (fopen_s, _access, ...); defining one of them makes clang warn
  "redeclared without 'dllimport'". That is expected for exactly these
  definitions, so the hooks of such names sit between a scoped pragma pair:

    #pragma clang diagnostic push
    #pragma clang diagnostic ignored "-Winconsistent-dllimport"
    ... the hooks and their HOOKABI_IMPORT_SLOT lines ...
    #pragma clang diagnostic pop

  A name the headers map onto a static mingw wrapper is not an import and
  gets no slot: `stat` is declared with the asm name stat64i32, defined in
  libmingwex, so the hook is `routine clink stat64i32` and its real function
  is the CRT export it wraps, _stat64i32.

  Finding the real function. HookReal(ASlot, AName) looks up the C runtime's
  definition: on Linux the next definition after the program
  (dlsym(RTLD_NEXT); libdl is linked by this unit), on Windows the export
  AName of ucrtbase.dll, the CRT zig's windows-gnu target links against
  (looked up there only: another loaded DLL such as msvcrt.dll can export a
  fopen with a different FILE). That on Linux RTLD_NEXT also finds names
  outside libc is incidental, not part of the contract. For a function of
  any other library, HookReal(ASlot, ALibrary, AName) looks AName up in that
  library, on both targets, if it is already loaded (it never loads one).

  A name that a static C runtime object defines inside the program has no
  export of that name to find: the hook's real function is what that object
  calls. HookABI.bindlist.h marks such names with an empty Real field. On
  Linux, zig's glibc link stub defines stat, fstat, lstat, stat64, fstat64
  and lstat64 in libc_nonshared, each as a call of __xstat, __fxstat,
  __lxstat, __xstat64, __fxstat64 or __lxstat64 with glibc's stat version
  as the first argument. Only glibc 2.33 and later exports stat itself;
  every glibc exports __xstat and its family. So a Linux stat hook resolves
  HookReal(ASlot, "__xstat") and calls it with HookStatVersion first:
  LReal(HookStatVersion, APath, ABuf). Windows stat follows the same rule
  through the mingw mapping above (stat64i32 -> _stat64i32).

  A header may give a name another symbol by asm label, and a definition
  then takes the label: glibc's headers name fscanf __isoc99_fscanf, and
  once __USE_FILE_OFFSET64 is defined they name stat stat64 (measured: the
  vendored minizip ioapi.h, which CustomIO imports, defines glibc's
  __USE_FILE_OFFSET64 itself, so in a unit importing CustomIO a
  <sys/stat.h> read after it makes `routine clink stat` define stat64
  while C code calls the plain stat). Such a hook is written in the unit's
  C++ under `__asm__("<name>")` for each symbol it must define (HookIO.pcpp
  defines stat and stat64 this way); `nm` of the linked program shows which
  symbols a hook defines.

  The run-time level: HookInstall writes a replacement into the import slot
  of a name in every loaded module (Linux the GOT entries of its JUMP_SLOT /
  GLOB_DAT relocations, read-only RELRO pages made writable for the store;
  Windows the import address table entries, under VirtualProtect), records
  each slot and what it held, and HookUninstall writes exactly that back
  into every recorded slot whose module is still loaded. Modules loaded
  later are patched as they load: Linux through the program's own dlopen
  (a hidden wrapper, never exported, so a shared library's own dlopen stays
  glibc's), Windows through the loader's DLL notification, which sees every
  load; unloads drop their slots. With nothing installed the wrappers are
  one atomic check. Calls that do not go through an import slot (inside the
  defining module, or a link-time hook's own symbol) are the link-time
  level's.
==============================================================================*/

module unit HookABI;

@ifdef TARGET_X86_64_LINUX_GNU
@linklibrary "dl";
@endif

// Public: the import slot of a hooked DLL function (see the unit header),
// written by the importer after its hook as `HOOKABI_IMPORT_SLOT(<fn>);`.
// Windows: a C-linkage pointer named __imp_<fn> holding the hook, declared
// first with extern "C" so the definition keeps C linkage. Elsewhere there
// is no import table, so it is a declaration that defines nothing; the
// caller's `;` ends it on both targets.
cpp header;

#if defined(_WIN32)
#define HOOKABI_IMPORT_SLOT(AName) \
  extern "C" decltype(&AName) __imp_##AName; \
  decltype(&AName) __imp_##AName = &AName
#else
#define HOOKABI_IMPORT_SLOT(AName) \
  static_assert(true, "HOOKABI_IMPORT_SLOT: no import slot on this target")
#endif

// Private: the lookup and the slot's atomic access, this unit's own
// translation unit. Helpers are named apart from the exported names (a body
// in the unit's namespace would find those first).
cpp source;

#include <atomic>
#include <cerrno>
#include <cstdint>
#include <cstring>
#include <mutex>
#include <new>
#include <string>
#include <vector>

#if defined(_WIN32)
#ifndef WIN32_LEAN_AND_MEAN
#define WIN32_LEAN_AND_MEAN
#endif
#ifndef NOMINMAX
#define NOMINMAX
#endif
#include <windows.h>
#include <psapi.h>
#else
#include <dlfcn.h>
#include <link.h>
#include <sys/mman.h>
#include <unistd.h>
#endif

// The longest library name HookDoInLibrary converts, in UTF-16 units with
// the terminator. A module name is a file name; a longer one is refused
// (nullptr) instead of allocating.
static constexpr int CHookLibraryNameMax = 512;

#if defined(_WIN32)

// AName's export in AModule, nullptr when the module or the export is
// missing. GetProcAddress gives a FARPROC; the slot stores it as void*.
static void* HookDoExport(HMODULE AModule, const char* AName)
{
  if ((AModule == nullptr) || (AName == nullptr))
    return nullptr;
  return reinterpret_cast<void*>(GetProcAddress(AModule, AName));
}

// The C runtime's definition: ucrtbase.dll, which the program imports
// (through the api-ms-win-crt-* sets) and so is loaded before any code
// runs. GetModuleHandleW never loads a module.
static void* HookDoNext(const char* AName)
{
  return HookDoExport(GetModuleHandleW(L"ucrtbase.dll"), AName);
}

// AName in an already loaded library, its name given as UTF-8. The name is
// converted into a stack buffer (no allocation); a name that does not
// convert (invalid UTF-8, too long) gives nullptr.
static void* HookDoInLibrary(const char* ALibrary, const char* AName)
{
  wchar_t LWide[CHookLibraryNameMax];
  int LCount;

  if (ALibrary == nullptr)
    return nullptr;
  LCount = MultiByteToWideChar(CP_UTF8, MB_ERR_INVALID_CHARS, ALibrary, -1,
    LWide, CHookLibraryNameMax);
  if (LCount == 0)
    return nullptr;
  return HookDoExport(GetModuleHandleW(LWide), AName);
}

#else

// The next definition of AName after the object that holds this code: the
// program itself in a link-time hook, so the result is the library's own
// function. nullptr when no later definition exists.
static void* HookDoNext(const char* AName)
{
  if (AName == nullptr)
    return nullptr;
  return dlsym(RTLD_NEXT, AName);
}

// AName in an already loaded library. RTLD_NOLOAD opens it only when it is
// loaded (and never runs its initializers again); the reference that open
// adds is dropped at once, the library stays loaded by whoever loaded it,
// so the address dlsym gave stays valid.
static void* HookDoInLibrary(const char* ALibrary, const char* AName)
{
  void* LHandle;
  void* LReal;

  if ((ALibrary == nullptr) || (AName == nullptr))
    return nullptr;
  LHandle = dlopen(ALibrary, RTLD_LAZY | RTLD_NOLOAD);
  if (LHandle == nullptr)
    return nullptr;
  LReal = dlsym(LHandle, AName);
  dlclose(LHandle);
  return LReal;
}

#endif

// Resolve once into the caller's slot. The slot is read with acquire and
// written with release through std::atomic_ref, so hooks entered at the same
// time on several threads all see either nullptr (and resolve: the lookup
// gives every one the same pointer) or the finished pointer. No lock: a hook
// may run inside the CRT itself. AInLibrary false = the C runtime's
// definition (HookDoNext, ALibrary unused), true = AName in ALibrary
// (HookDoInLibrary; a nil ALibrary then gives nullptr, never the CRT).
static void* HookDoReal(void*& ASlot, const char* ALibrary, const char* AName,
  bool AInLibrary)
{
  std::atomic_ref<void*> LSlot(ASlot);
  void* LReal = LSlot.load(std::memory_order_acquire);
  if (LReal == nullptr)
  {
    if (AInLibrary)
      LReal = HookDoInLibrary(ALibrary, AName);
    else
      LReal = HookDoNext(AName);
    if (LReal != nullptr)
      LSlot.store(LReal, std::memory_order_release);
  }
  return LReal;
}

// The run-time level (HookInstall / HookUninstall). An install = one name and
// its replacement, with every import slot it wrote: the slot, what it held,
// the module it belongs to (load address + name, so a module that went away
// is never written again). Two locks: HookDoRunLock makes installs,
// uninstalls and (Linux) the load hooks' passes run one at a time, and may
// be held while the loader's lock is taken; HookDoTableLock guards the
// install list and every install's slots, and is never held while the
// loader's lock is taken (the Windows DLL notification takes it inside the
// loader's lock). Order: run lock, loader, table lock.

// One import slot an install wrote. ReadOnly: the slot's page is read-only
// between writes (Linux RELRO, Windows a read-only import table page).
struct HookDoSlot
{
  void** Address = nullptr;
  void* Old = nullptr;
  std::uintptr_t Base = 0;
  std::string Module;
  bool ReadOnly = false;
};

// Removing: the uninstall is putting the slots back; a module loaded now is
// not patched with it
struct HookDoInstall
{
  std::string Name;
  void* Replacement = nullptr;
  std::vector<HookDoSlot> Slots;
  bool Removing = false;
};

static std::mutex& HookDoRunLock()
{
  static std::mutex LLock;
  return LLock;
}

static std::mutex& HookDoTableLock()
{
  static std::mutex LLock;
  return LLock;
}

static std::vector<HookDoInstall*>& HookDoInstalls()
{
  static std::vector<HookDoInstall*> LInstalls;
  return LInstalls;
}

// How many installs exist, read by the load hooks without the lock
static std::atomic<int> HookDoInstallCount{0};

// True when the install already recorded AAddress
static bool HookDoKnownSlot(const HookDoInstall& AInstall, void** AAddress)
{
  for (const HookDoSlot& LSlot : AInstall.Slots)
  {
    if (LSlot.Address == AAddress)
      return true;
  }
  return false;
}

// The install record of AState among the installs, nullptr when it is not one
static HookDoInstall* HookDoFindInstall(const void* AState)
{
  for (HookDoInstall* LInstall : HookDoInstalls())
  {
    if (LInstall == AState)
      return LInstall;
  }
  return nullptr;
}

#if !defined(_WIN32)

// The system page size, for mprotect
static std::uintptr_t HookDoPageSize()
{
  static const std::uintptr_t LSize = static_cast<std::uintptr_t>(sysconf(_SC_PAGESIZE));
  return LSize;
}

// Stores AValue in the slot. A slot in a read-only page is made writable for
// the store and read-only again after it. False when the page cannot be made
// writable (nothing is written then).
static bool HookDoWriteSlot(void** AAddress, void* AValue, const bool AReadOnly)
{
  const std::uintptr_t LPage = HookDoPageSize();
  void* LStart = reinterpret_cast<void*>(reinterpret_cast<std::uintptr_t>(AAddress) & ~(LPage - 1));

  if (AReadOnly && (mprotect(LStart, LPage, PROT_READ | PROT_WRITE) != 0))
    return false;
  std::atomic_ref<void*>(*AAddress).store(AValue, std::memory_order_release);
  if (AReadOnly)
    mprotect(LStart, LPage, PROT_READ);
  return true;
}

// The tables a loaded object's import slots are found by. ReadOnlyStart /
// ReadOnlyEnd: the pages the loader made read-only (PT_GNU_RELRO, both ends
// rounded down to a page, as glibc protects it).
struct HookDoTables
{
  const ElfW(Sym)* Symbols = nullptr;
  const char* Strings = nullptr;
  const ElfW(Rela)* Plt = nullptr;
  std::size_t PltSize = 0;
  const ElfW(Rela)* Rela = nullptr;
  std::size_t RelaSize = 0;
  std::uintptr_t ReadOnlyStart = 0;
  std::uintptr_t ReadOnlyEnd = 0;
};

// An address from a dynamic section: glibc rewrites them to absolute
// addresses in every object it loaded, but not in the vDSO, where a value
// below the load address is still an offset from it
static std::uintptr_t HookDoDynamicAddress(const std::uintptr_t ABase, const ElfW(Addr) AValue)
{
  if (AValue < ABase)
    return ABase + AValue;
  return AValue;
}

// AInfo's tables; false when the object has no dynamic symbols
static bool HookDoReadTables(const struct dl_phdr_info* AInfo, HookDoTables& ATables)
{
  const ElfW(Dyn)* LDynamic = nullptr;
  const std::uintptr_t LPage = HookDoPageSize();
  const std::uintptr_t LBase = AInfo->dlpi_addr;

  for (ElfW(Half) LI = 0; LI < AInfo->dlpi_phnum; ++LI)
  {
    const ElfW(Phdr)& LHeader = AInfo->dlpi_phdr[LI];
    if (LHeader.p_type == PT_DYNAMIC)
      LDynamic = reinterpret_cast<const ElfW(Dyn)*>(LBase + LHeader.p_vaddr);
    else if (LHeader.p_type == PT_GNU_RELRO)
    {
      ATables.ReadOnlyStart = (LBase + LHeader.p_vaddr) & ~(LPage - 1);
      ATables.ReadOnlyEnd = (LBase + LHeader.p_vaddr + LHeader.p_memsz) & ~(LPage - 1);
    }
  }
  if (LDynamic == nullptr)
    return false;
  for (const ElfW(Dyn)* LEntry = LDynamic; LEntry->d_tag != DT_NULL; ++LEntry)
  {
    if (LEntry->d_tag == DT_SYMTAB)
      ATables.Symbols = reinterpret_cast<const ElfW(Sym)*>(HookDoDynamicAddress(LBase, LEntry->d_un.d_ptr));
    else if (LEntry->d_tag == DT_STRTAB)
      ATables.Strings = reinterpret_cast<const char*>(HookDoDynamicAddress(LBase, LEntry->d_un.d_ptr));
    else if (LEntry->d_tag == DT_JMPREL)
      ATables.Plt = reinterpret_cast<const ElfW(Rela)*>(HookDoDynamicAddress(LBase, LEntry->d_un.d_ptr));
    else if (LEntry->d_tag == DT_PLTRELSZ)
      ATables.PltSize = LEntry->d_un.d_val;
    else if (LEntry->d_tag == DT_RELA)
      ATables.Rela = reinterpret_cast<const ElfW(Rela)*>(HookDoDynamicAddress(LBase, LEntry->d_un.d_ptr));
    else if (LEntry->d_tag == DT_RELASZ)
      ATables.RelaSize = LEntry->d_un.d_val;
  }
  return (ATables.Symbols != nullptr) && (ATables.Strings != nullptr);
}

// Every import slot of AInstall's name in one object (a JUMP_SLOT: a call
// through the PLT; a GLOB_DAT: the function's address taken or a no-PLT
// call) that the install has not written yet: recorded, then written with
// the replacement. False when a write failed (that slot is not recorded;
// the ones written before it are, so they restore).
static bool HookDoPatchTables(HookDoInstall& AInstall, const struct dl_phdr_info* AInfo,
  const HookDoTables& ATables)
{
  const ElfW(Rela)* const LLists[2] = { ATables.Plt, ATables.Rela };
  const std::size_t LCounts[2] = { ATables.PltSize / sizeof(ElfW(Rela)),
    ATables.RelaSize / sizeof(ElfW(Rela)) };
  const std::uintptr_t LPage = HookDoPageSize();

  for (int LList = 0; LList < 2; ++LList)
  {
    if (LLists[LList] == nullptr)
      continue;
    for (std::size_t LI = 0; LI < LCounts[LList]; ++LI)
    {
      const ElfW(Rela)& LEntry = LLists[LList][LI];
      const auto LType = ELF64_R_TYPE(LEntry.r_info);
      const auto LSymbol = ELF64_R_SYM(LEntry.r_info);
      if (((LType != R_X86_64_JUMP_SLOT) && (LType != R_X86_64_GLOB_DAT)) || (LSymbol == 0))
        continue;
      if (std::strcmp(ATables.Strings + ATables.Symbols[LSymbol].st_name, AInstall.Name.c_str()) != 0)
        continue;
      void** const LAddress = reinterpret_cast<void**>(AInfo->dlpi_addr + LEntry.r_offset);
      if (HookDoKnownSlot(AInstall, LAddress))
        continue;
      const std::uintptr_t LSlotPage = reinterpret_cast<std::uintptr_t>(LAddress) & ~(LPage - 1);
      HookDoSlot LSlot;
      LSlot.Address = LAddress;
      LSlot.Old = std::atomic_ref<void*>(*LAddress).load(std::memory_order_acquire);
      LSlot.Base = AInfo->dlpi_addr;
      LSlot.Module = (AInfo->dlpi_name != nullptr) ? AInfo->dlpi_name : "";
      LSlot.ReadOnly = (LSlotPage >= ATables.ReadOnlyStart) && (LSlotPage < ATables.ReadOnlyEnd);
      AInstall.Slots.push_back(LSlot);
      if (!HookDoWriteSlot(LAddress, AInstall.Replacement, LSlot.ReadOnly))
      {
        AInstall.Slots.pop_back();
        return false;
      }
    }
  }
  return true;
}

// dl_iterate_phdr runs these with the loader's lock held, so no object goes
// away while its slots are read or written
struct HookDoPatchScan
{
  HookDoInstall* Install = nullptr;
  bool Ok = true;
};

static int HookDoPatchObject(struct dl_phdr_info* AInfo, std::size_t, void* AData)
{
  HookDoPatchScan& LScan = *static_cast<HookDoPatchScan*>(AData);
  HookDoTables LTables;

  try
  {
    if (!HookDoReadTables(AInfo, LTables))
      return 0;
    std::lock_guard<std::mutex> LGuard(HookDoTableLock());
    if (LScan.Install->Removing)
      return 1;
    if (!HookDoPatchTables(*LScan.Install, AInfo, LTables))
    {
      LScan.Ok = false;
      return 1;
    }
  }
  catch (...)
  {
    LScan.Ok = false;
    return 1;
  }
  return 0;
}

// Present / Restored: per slot of Install, whether its module is still
// loaded, and (ARestore) whether the old value went back
struct HookDoSlotScan
{
  HookDoInstall* Install = nullptr;
  bool Restore = false;
  std::vector<char> Present;
  std::vector<char> Restored;
};

static int HookDoVisitObject(struct dl_phdr_info* AInfo, std::size_t, void* AData)
{
  HookDoSlotScan& LScan = *static_cast<HookDoSlotScan*>(AData);
  const char* LName = (AInfo->dlpi_name != nullptr) ? AInfo->dlpi_name : "";

  try
  {
    std::lock_guard<std::mutex> LGuard(HookDoTableLock());
    for (std::size_t LI = 0; LI < LScan.Install->Slots.size(); ++LI)
    {
      const HookDoSlot& LSlot = LScan.Install->Slots[LI];
      if ((LSlot.Base != AInfo->dlpi_addr) || (LSlot.Module != LName))
        continue;
      LScan.Present[LI] = 1;
      if (LScan.Restore && (LScan.Restored[LI] == 0))
        LScan.Restored[LI] = HookDoWriteSlot(LSlot.Address, LSlot.Old, LSlot.ReadOnly) ? 1 : 0;
    }
  }
  catch (...)
  {
    // The lock could not be taken: this module's slots stay as they are
  }
  return 0;
}

// Drops every slot whose module is gone; with ARestore, writes the others
// back first. True when no slot is left (with ARestore: all went back). The
// caller holds the run lock, not the table lock.
static bool HookDoVisitSlots(HookDoInstall& AInstall, const bool ARestore)
{
  HookDoSlotScan LScan;
  std::vector<HookDoSlot> LKept;

  LScan.Install = &AInstall;
  LScan.Restore = ARestore;
  {
    std::lock_guard<std::mutex> LGuard(HookDoTableLock());
    LScan.Present.assign(AInstall.Slots.size(), 0);
    LScan.Restored.assign(AInstall.Slots.size(), 0);
  }
  dl_iterate_phdr(HookDoVisitObject, &LScan);
  std::lock_guard<std::mutex> LGuard(HookDoTableLock());
  for (std::size_t LI = 0; LI < AInstall.Slots.size(); ++LI)
  {
    // Kept: still loaded, and (restoring) not yet written back
    if ((LScan.Present[LI] != 0) && ((!ARestore) || (LScan.Restored[LI] == 0)))
      LKept.push_back(AInstall.Slots[LI]);
  }
  AInstall.Slots.swap(LKept);
  return (!ARestore) || AInstall.Slots.empty();
}

// Writes AInstall into every loaded object; false when a slot could not be
// written (the ones that were stay recorded)
static bool HookDoApply(HookDoInstall& AInstall)
{
  HookDoPatchScan LScan;

  LScan.Install = &AInstall;
  dl_iterate_phdr(HookDoPatchObject, &LScan);
  return LScan.Ok;
}

// The function a name's slots resolve to when nothing is hooked
static void* HookDoOriginal(const char* AName)
{
  return dlsym(RTLD_DEFAULT, AName);
}

#else

// Stores AValue in an import address table entry: the page made writable for
// the store, its protection put back after it. False when the protection
// cannot be changed (nothing written then).
static bool HookDoWriteSlot(void** AAddress, void* AValue, const bool)
{
  DWORD LOld = 0;
  DWORD LUnused = 0;

  if (!VirtualProtect(AAddress, sizeof(void*), PAGE_READWRITE, &LOld))
    return false;
  std::atomic_ref<void*>(*AAddress).store(AValue, std::memory_order_release);
  VirtualProtect(AAddress, sizeof(void*), LOld, &LUnused);
  return true;
}

// Every loaded module, in load order; empty when they cannot be listed
static std::vector<HMODULE> HookDoModules()
{
  std::vector<HMODULE> LModules(256);
  DWORD LNeeded = 0;

  for (int LTry = 0; LTry < 4; ++LTry)
  {
    if (!K32EnumProcessModules(GetCurrentProcess(), LModules.data(),
      static_cast<DWORD>(LModules.size() * sizeof(HMODULE)), &LNeeded))
      return std::vector<HMODULE>();
    if (LNeeded <= (LModules.size() * sizeof(HMODULE)))
    {
      LModules.resize(LNeeded / sizeof(HMODULE));
      return LModules;
    }
    LModules.resize((LNeeded / sizeof(HMODULE)) + 16);
  }
  return std::vector<HMODULE>();
}

// The module containing AAddress, its load count raised so it cannot unload
// until HookDoUnpin; nullptr when no loaded module contains it
static HMODULE HookDoPin(const void* AAddress)
{
  HMODULE LModule = nullptr;

  if (!GetModuleHandleExW(GET_MODULE_HANDLE_EX_FLAG_FROM_ADDRESS,
    static_cast<LPCWSTR>(AAddress), &LModule))
    return nullptr;
  return LModule;
}

static void HookDoUnpin(const HMODULE AModule)
{
  if (AModule != nullptr)
    FreeLibrary(AModule);
}

// Calls AVisit(slot address) for every import address table entry of AName
// in AModule (imported by name, from any DLL). The module must stay loaded
// meanwhile (pinned, or inside the loader's notification). AVisit returns
// false to stop; the result is false then.
template <typename TVisit>
static bool HookDoEachImport(const HMODULE AModule, const char* AName, TVisit&& AVisit)
{
  const unsigned char* LBase = reinterpret_cast<const unsigned char*>(AModule);
  const auto* LDos = reinterpret_cast<const IMAGE_DOS_HEADER*>(LBase);

  if ((LBase == nullptr) || (LDos->e_magic != IMAGE_DOS_SIGNATURE))
    return true;
  const auto* LNt = reinterpret_cast<const IMAGE_NT_HEADERS64*>(LBase + LDos->e_lfanew);
  if ((LNt->Signature != IMAGE_NT_SIGNATURE) ||
    (LNt->OptionalHeader.Magic != IMAGE_NT_OPTIONAL_HDR64_MAGIC))
    return true;
  const IMAGE_DATA_DIRECTORY& LDirectory =
    LNt->OptionalHeader.DataDirectory[IMAGE_DIRECTORY_ENTRY_IMPORT];
  if ((LDirectory.VirtualAddress == 0) || (LDirectory.Size == 0))
    return true;
  for (const auto* LImport = reinterpret_cast<const IMAGE_IMPORT_DESCRIPTOR*>(LBase +
    LDirectory.VirtualAddress); LImport->Name != 0; ++LImport)
  {
    // Without its name table a descriptor's entries cannot be told apart
    if (LImport->OriginalFirstThunk == 0)
      continue;
    const auto* LNames = reinterpret_cast<const IMAGE_THUNK_DATA64*>(LBase + LImport->OriginalFirstThunk);
    auto* LSlots = reinterpret_cast<IMAGE_THUNK_DATA64*>(const_cast<unsigned char*>(LBase) +
      LImport->FirstThunk);
    for (; LNames->u1.AddressOfData != 0; ++LNames, ++LSlots)
    {
      if (IMAGE_SNAP_BY_ORDINAL64(LNames->u1.Ordinal))
        continue;
      const auto* LByName = reinterpret_cast<const IMAGE_IMPORT_BY_NAME*>(LBase +
        LNames->u1.AddressOfData);
      if (std::strcmp(reinterpret_cast<const char*>(LByName->Name), AName) != 0)
        continue;
      if (!AVisit(reinterpret_cast<void**>(&LSlots->u1.Function)))
        return false;
    }
  }
  return true;
}

// Every not yet recorded import slot of AInstall's name in AModule: recorded,
// then written with the replacement. The caller holds the table lock and
// keeps AModule loaded. False when a write failed (that slot unrecorded).
static bool HookDoPatchModule(HookDoInstall& AInstall, const HMODULE AModule)
{
  if (AInstall.Removing)
    return true;
  return HookDoEachImport(AModule, AInstall.Name.c_str(), [&](void** AAddress)
  {
    if (HookDoKnownSlot(AInstall, AAddress))
      return true;
    HookDoSlot LSlot;
    LSlot.Address = AAddress;
    LSlot.Old = std::atomic_ref<void*>(*AAddress).load(std::memory_order_acquire);
    LSlot.Base = reinterpret_cast<std::uintptr_t>(AModule);
    AInstall.Slots.push_back(LSlot);
    if (!HookDoWriteSlot(AAddress, AInstall.Replacement, false))
    {
      AInstall.Slots.pop_back();
      return false;
    }
    return true;
  });
}

// Writes AInstall into every loaded module, each pinned meanwhile; false when
// a slot could not be written (the ones that were stay recorded)
static bool HookDoApply(HookDoInstall& AInstall)
{
  bool LOk = true;

  for (const HMODULE LListed : HookDoModules())
  {
    const HMODULE LModule = HookDoPin(LListed);
    if (LModule == nullptr)
      continue;
    {
      std::lock_guard<std::mutex> LGuard(HookDoTableLock());
      if (!HookDoPatchModule(AInstall, LModule))
        LOk = false;
    }
    HookDoUnpin(LModule);
    if (!LOk)
      break;
  }
  return LOk;
}

// Drops every slot whose module is gone; with ARestore, writes the others
// back first, each with its module pinned (and, once pinned, still recorded:
// a module that unloaded meanwhile had its slots dropped by the
// notification). True when no slot is left (with ARestore: all went back).
// The caller holds the run lock, not the table lock.
static bool HookDoVisitSlots(HookDoInstall& AInstall, const bool ARestore)
{
  std::vector<void**> LAddresses;

  {
    std::lock_guard<std::mutex> LGuard(HookDoTableLock());
    for (const HookDoSlot& LSlot : AInstall.Slots)
      LAddresses.push_back(LSlot.Address);
  }
  for (void** LAddress : LAddresses)
  {
    const HMODULE LModule = HookDoPin(LAddress);
    std::lock_guard<std::mutex> LGuard(HookDoTableLock());
    for (auto LCursor = AInstall.Slots.begin(); LCursor != AInstall.Slots.end(); ++LCursor)
    {
      if (LCursor->Address != LAddress)
        continue;
      if ((LModule == nullptr) || (reinterpret_cast<std::uintptr_t>(LModule) != LCursor->Base))
        AInstall.Slots.erase(LCursor);
      else if (ARestore && HookDoWriteSlot(LCursor->Address, LCursor->Old, false))
        AInstall.Slots.erase(LCursor);
      break;
    }
    HookDoUnpin(LModule);
  }
  std::lock_guard<std::mutex> LGuard(HookDoTableLock());
  return (!ARestore) || AInstall.Slots.empty();
}

// The function AName's slots reach: the current value of the first import
// slot of it in load order; when no module imports it yet, the first module
// that exports it
static void* HookDoOriginal(const char* AName)
{
  const std::vector<HMODULE> LModules = HookDoModules();
  void* LFound = nullptr;

  for (const HMODULE LListed : LModules)
  {
    const HMODULE LModule = HookDoPin(LListed);
    if (LModule == nullptr)
      continue;
    HookDoEachImport(LModule, AName, [&](void** AAddress)
    {
      LFound = std::atomic_ref<void*>(*AAddress).load(std::memory_order_acquire);
      return false;
    });
    HookDoUnpin(LModule);
    if (LFound != nullptr)
      return LFound;
  }
  for (const HMODULE LListed : LModules)
  {
    LFound = HookDoExport(LListed, AName);
    if (LFound != nullptr)
      return LFound;
  }
  return nullptr;
}

#endif

// Registers the Windows load notification (nothing to do on Linux: the
// dlopen / dlclose wrappers are always in place). Declared here, defined
// with the per-target run-time code below.
#if defined(_WIN32)
static bool HookDoEnsureNotification();
#else
static bool HookDoEnsureNotification()
{
  return true;
}
#endif

// HookInstall: AName's slots in every loaded module take AReplacement.
// AOriginal / AState are the caller's Hook record. False with errno: EINVAL
// (nil or empty name, nil replacement), EEXIST (this record or another one
// already has AName installed), ENOENT (no loaded module defines AName),
// EACCES (a slot could not be written: every slot written is put back),
// ENOMEM.
static bool HookDoInstallName(const char* AName, void* AReplacement, void*& AOriginal,
  void*& AState)
{
  HookDoInstall* LInstall = nullptr;
  bool LJoined = false;
  void* LOriginal;

  if ((AName == nullptr) || (AName[0] == '\0') || (AReplacement == nullptr))
  {
    errno = EINVAL;
    return false;
  }
  if (AState != nullptr)
  {
    errno = EEXIST;
    return false;
  }
  try
  {
    std::lock_guard<std::mutex> LGuard(HookDoRunLock());
    {
      std::lock_guard<std::mutex> LTable(HookDoTableLock());
      for (const HookDoInstall* LOther : HookDoInstalls())
      {
        if (LOther->Name == AName)
        {
          errno = EEXIST;
          return false;
        }
      }
    }
    LOriginal = HookDoOriginal(AName);
    if (LOriginal == nullptr)
    {
      errno = ENOENT;
      return false;
    }
    // The Windows load notification must be in place before this install can
    // join: a DLL loaded after it joins is only patched by the notification
    HookDoEnsureNotification();
    LInstall = new HookDoInstall();
    LInstall->Name = AName;
    LInstall->Replacement = AReplacement;
    {
      // Joined and counted before the apply, so a module loaded during it is
      // patched by the load hook with this install, never missed
      std::lock_guard<std::mutex> LTable(HookDoTableLock());
      HookDoInstalls().push_back(LInstall);
      HookDoInstallCount.fetch_add(1);
      LJoined = true;
    }
    if (!HookDoApply(*LInstall))
    {
      LInstall->Removing = true;
      HookDoVisitSlots(*LInstall, true);
      std::lock_guard<std::mutex> LTable(HookDoTableLock());
      for (auto LCursor = HookDoInstalls().begin(); LCursor != HookDoInstalls().end(); ++LCursor)
      {
        if (*LCursor == LInstall)
        {
          HookDoInstalls().erase(LCursor);
          break;
        }
      }
      HookDoInstallCount.fetch_sub(1);
      delete LInstall;
      errno = EACCES;
      return false;
    }
  }
  catch (...)
  {
    // Out of memory before the record joined the list: nothing was written
    if ((LInstall != nullptr) && (!LJoined))
      delete LInstall;
    errno = ENOMEM;
    return false;
  }
  AOriginal = LOriginal;
  AState = LInstall;
  return true;
}

// HookUninstall: every slot whose module is still loaded gets back what it
// held; AState becomes nil, AOriginal stays (a replacement still running on
// another thread may call it). False with errno: EINVAL (not installed),
// EACCES (a slot could not be written back: still installed, the slots that
// did go back are done), ENOMEM.
static bool HookDoUninstallState(void*& AState)
{
  HookDoInstall* LInstall;

  if (AState == nullptr)
  {
    errno = EINVAL;
    return false;
  }
  try
  {
    std::lock_guard<std::mutex> LGuard(HookDoRunLock());
    {
      std::lock_guard<std::mutex> LTable(HookDoTableLock());
      LInstall = HookDoFindInstall(AState);
      // Removing: a load hook running now does not patch it back in while the
      // restore pass is putting slots back
      if (LInstall != nullptr)
        LInstall->Removing = true;
    }
    if (LInstall == nullptr)
    {
      errno = EINVAL;
      return false;
    }
    if (!HookDoVisitSlots(*LInstall, true))
    {
      // Still installed: a later uninstall (or this one retried) finishes it
      std::lock_guard<std::mutex> LTable(HookDoTableLock());
      LInstall->Removing = false;
      errno = EACCES;
      return false;
    }
    std::lock_guard<std::mutex> LTable(HookDoTableLock());
    for (auto LCursor = HookDoInstalls().begin(); LCursor != HookDoInstalls().end(); ++LCursor)
    {
      if (*LCursor == LInstall)
      {
        HookDoInstalls().erase(LCursor);
        break;
      }
    }
    delete LInstall;
    HookDoInstallCount.fetch_sub(1);
  }
  catch (...)
  {
    errno = ENOMEM;
    return false;
  }
  AState = nullptr;
  return true;
}

#if !defined(_WIN32)

// Linux, after the program's own outermost dlopen returns (the loader lock
// is released then, so the run lock is safe to take): every install into the
// modules that came with the load. A slot that cannot be written there is
// left as the loader set it (no caller to tell: the load itself succeeded).
// The install list changes only under the run lock, held here.
static void HookDoReapply()
{
  if (HookDoInstallCount.load() == 0)
    return;
  try
  {
    std::lock_guard<std::mutex> LGuard(HookDoRunLock());
    for (HookDoInstall* LInstall : HookDoInstalls())
      HookDoApply(*LInstall);
  }
  catch (...)
  {
  }
}

// Linux, after the outermost dlclose: slots of modules that went away are
// forgotten
static void HookDoPrune()
{
  if (HookDoInstallCount.load() == 0)
    return;
  try
  {
    std::lock_guard<std::mutex> LGuard(HookDoRunLock());
    for (HookDoInstall* LInstall : HookDoInstalls())
      HookDoVisitSlots(*LInstall, false);
  }
  catch (...)
  {
  }
}

#endif

#if defined(_WIN32)

// Windows: LdrRegisterDllNotification tells us of every DLL load and unload
// (ntdll, resolved once). The callback runs inside the loader lock, so it
// takes the table lock only (never the run lock) and never loads or frees a
// module. A load of the named DLL re-applies the installs into it; an unload
// prunes the slots of modules that went away.

#define LDR_DLL_NOTIFICATION_REASON_LOADED 1
#define LDR_DLL_NOTIFICATION_REASON_UNLOADED 2

// LDR_DLL_LOADED_NOTIFICATION_DATA (the unloaded form has the same layout).
// The two names are PCUNICODE_STRINGs, never read here: kept as pointers of
// the same size so DllBase sits where the loader writes it.
struct HookDoNotificationData
{
  ULONG Flags;
  const void* FullDllName;
  const void* BaseDllName;
  PVOID DllBase;
  ULONG SizeOfImage;
};

using HookDoNotificationFn = VOID (CALLBACK*)(ULONG, const HookDoNotificationData*, PVOID);
// The result is an NTSTATUS (a LONG, 0 = success; its header is not included)
using HookDoRegisterFn = LONG (NTAPI*)(ULONG, HookDoNotificationFn, PVOID, PVOID*);

static PVOID GHookDoNotificationCookie = nullptr;

// Only the module the notification names is touched: one being loaded is
// patched (it cannot unload while the loader holds its lock), one unloading
// has its slots dropped. No module is listed, pinned or freed here.
static VOID CALLBACK HookDoNotification(ULONG AReason, const HookDoNotificationData* AData, PVOID)
{
  if ((HookDoInstallCount.load() == 0) || (AData == nullptr) || (AData->DllBase == nullptr))
    return;
  try
  {
    const HMODULE LModule = static_cast<HMODULE>(AData->DllBase);
    const std::uintptr_t LBase = reinterpret_cast<std::uintptr_t>(AData->DllBase);
    std::lock_guard<std::mutex> LGuard(HookDoTableLock());
    for (HookDoInstall* LInstall : HookDoInstalls())
    {
      if (AReason == LDR_DLL_NOTIFICATION_REASON_LOADED)
        HookDoPatchModule(*LInstall, LModule);
      else if (AReason == LDR_DLL_NOTIFICATION_REASON_UNLOADED)
      {
        std::vector<HookDoSlot>& LSlots = LInstall->Slots;
        for (auto LCursor = LSlots.begin(); LCursor != LSlots.end(); )
        {
          if (LCursor->Base == LBase)
            LCursor = LSlots.erase(LCursor);
          else
            ++LCursor;
        }
      }
    }
  }
  catch (...)
  {
    // Out of memory recording a slot: that module keeps the loader's value
  }
}

// Registers the notification once (the first install). True when it is in
// place; false leaves the install to patch only the modules loaded now
// (later loads are not caught). The caller holds the run lock.
static bool HookDoEnsureNotification()
{
  static std::atomic<bool> LRegistered{false};
  HMODULE LNtdll;
  HookDoRegisterFn LRegister;

  if (LRegistered.load(std::memory_order_acquire))
    return true;
  LNtdll = GetModuleHandleW(L"ntdll.dll");
  if (LNtdll == nullptr)
    return false;
  LRegister = reinterpret_cast<HookDoRegisterFn>(
    reinterpret_cast<void*>(GetProcAddress(LNtdll, "LdrRegisterDllNotification")));
  if (LRegister == nullptr)
    return false;
  if (LRegister(0, HookDoNotification, nullptr, &GHookDoNotificationCookie) != 0)
    return false;
  LRegistered.store(true, std::memory_order_release);
  return true;
}

#else

// The program's own dlopen / dlclose (link-time hooks, hidden: never
// exported, so a shared library's own dlopen calls stay glibc's, which finds
// the caller's RUNPATH / $ORIGIN by the caller's address). The installs are
// re-applied or pruned when the outermost call of the thread returns: a
// library constructor's nested dlopen runs inside the loader's lock, and
// taking HookDoRunLock there could deadlock against a HookInstall waiting on
// the loader.
static thread_local int GHookDoLoadDepth = 0;
static void* GHookDoRealDlopen = nullptr;
static void* GHookDoRealDlclose = nullptr;

extern "C" __attribute__((visibility("hidden"))) void* HookDoDlopen(const char* AFile, int AMode)
  __asm__("dlopen");

extern "C" __attribute__((visibility("hidden"))) void* HookDoDlopen(const char* AFile, int AMode)
{
  using TReal = void* (*)(const char*, int);
  TReal LReal;
  void* LHandle;

  LReal = reinterpret_cast<TReal>(HookDoReal(GHookDoRealDlopen, nullptr, "dlopen", false));
  if (LReal == nullptr)
    return nullptr;
  ++GHookDoLoadDepth;
  LHandle = LReal(AFile, AMode);
  --GHookDoLoadDepth;
  if ((LHandle != nullptr) && (GHookDoLoadDepth == 0))
    HookDoReapply();
  return LHandle;
}

extern "C" __attribute__((visibility("hidden"))) int HookDoDlclose(void* AHandle)
  __asm__("dlclose");

extern "C" __attribute__((visibility("hidden"))) int HookDoDlclose(void* AHandle)
{
  using TReal = int (*)(void*);
  TReal LReal;
  int LResult;

  LReal = reinterpret_cast<TReal>(HookDoReal(GHookDoRealDlclose, nullptr, "dlclose", false));
  if (LReal == nullptr)
    return -1;
  ++GHookDoLoadDepth;
  LResult = LReal(AHandle);
  --GHookDoLoadDepth;
  if (GHookDoLoadDepth == 0)
    HookDoPrune();
  return LResult;
}

#endif

@ifdef TARGET_X86_64_LINUX_GNU
exported const
  /// glibc's stat version on x86_64 (_STAT_VER, which the glibc headers zig
  /// ships do not define): the first argument of __xstat, __fxstat, __lxstat,
  /// __xstat64, __fxstat64 and __lxstat64, the real functions of a Linux
  /// stat-family hook (see "Finding the real function" in the unit header).
  /// Linux only.
  /// @example `return LReal(HookStatVersion, APath, ABuf);`
  /// @since 0.2
  HookStatVersion: int32 = 1;
@endif

/// Finds the real function a link-time hook of a C runtime name stands in
/// for: on Linux the next definition of AName after the program
/// (dlsym(RTLD_NEXT)), on Windows the export AName of ucrtbase.dll. The first
/// call resolves it into ASlot; later calls read ASlot (one atomic load), so a
/// hook may call this on every entry. Safe on several threads at once, and it
/// never allocates, so it is safe inside the CRT and before the program
/// starts.
/// @param ASlot the hook's own pointer, nil until the first call; keep one per
///   hooked name, at module level
/// @param AName the real function's C name: the hooked name, or, for a name
///   a static C runtime object defines (an empty Real in HookABI.bindlist.h),
///   the function that object calls (Linux: hook stat, real "__xstat", called
///   with HookStatVersion first; Windows: hook stat64i32, real "_stat64i32")
/// @returns the real function, to be cast to the hook's routine type with
///   reinterpret_cast; nil when the C runtime has no AName (the slot stays nil
///   and the next call looks again): the hook must not call it then
/// @example `LReal := reinterpret_cast<FopenFn>(HookReal(GRealFopen, "fopen"));`
/// @see HookReal(ASlot, ALibrary, AName) for a function of another library
/// @since 0.2
exported routine HookReal(var ASlot: ptr; const AName: ptr to const char): ptr;
begin
  return HookDoReal(ASlot, nil, AName, false);
end;

/// Finds the real function of a hooked name in one named library, for a
/// function outside the C runtime (a Win32 API in kernel32.dll, a function
/// of a shared library). The library must already be loaded: this never
/// loads one (Windows GetModuleHandleW, Linux dlopen with RTLD_NOLOAD). The
/// first call resolves into ASlot, later calls read it, as the two-argument
/// form; safe on several threads at once. On Linux the first call goes
/// through the dynamic loader (dlopen / dlclose), so a hook that the loader
/// itself may enter (malloc and its family) resolves with the two-argument
/// form instead.
/// @param ASlot the hook's own pointer, nil until the first call; keep one per
///   hooked name, at module level
/// @param ALibrary the library's file name, UTF-8 (Windows: "kernel32.dll";
///   Linux: the soname, "libc.so.6")
/// @param AName the real function's C name
/// @returns the real function, to be cast to the hook's routine type with
///   reinterpret_cast; nil when the library is not loaded or has no AName (the
///   slot stays nil and the next call looks again): the hook must not call it
///   then
/// @example `LReal := reinterpret_cast<GetAttrFn>(HookReal(GRealGetAttr, "kernel32.dll", "GetFileAttributesA"));`
/// @see HookReal(ASlot, AName) for a C runtime name
/// @since 0.2
exported routine HookReal(var ASlot: ptr; const ALibrary: ptr to const char; const AName: ptr to const char): ptr;
begin
  return HookDoReal(ASlot, ALibrary, AName, true);
end;

/// A run-time hook, filled by HookInstall: while installed, every call of
/// the hooked name through a module's import slot (Linux a GOT entry, Windows
/// an import address table entry) reaches the replacement instead. A Hook
/// variable starts zeroed (not installed); keep it while installed.
/// @see HookInstall
/// @see HookUninstall
/// @since 0.2
exported type
  Hook = record
    /// The function the hooked name's slots reached before the install (the
    /// replacement calls it for the real work; calling the name itself from
    /// the replacement would reach the replacement again). Stays valid after
    /// HookUninstall: a replacement still running on another thread may call
    /// it.
    Original: ptr;
    /// HookABI's record of the install; nil when not installed
    State: ptr;
  end;

/// Installs a run-time hook: AName's import slot in every module loaded now
/// takes AReplacement, and so does every module the program loads later
/// (Linux: through the program's own dlopen; Windows: by the loader's DLL
/// notification). Code that calls AName directly, not through an import slot
/// (the module that defines it, a link-time hook), is not reached: that is
/// the link-time level's job. One install per name at a time. Thread-safe;
/// installs and uninstalls run one at a time.
/// @param AHook the record to fill: zeroed, or uninstalled
/// @param AName the function's C name, as the modules import it
/// @param AReplacement a function of the same C signature and calling
///   convention (a `routine clink`, cast to ptr)
/// @returns true when installed (AHook.Original and AHook.State set; a name
///   no module imports yet is installed for the modules loaded later); false
///   with errno: EINVAL (nil or empty AName, nil AReplacement), EEXIST (AHook
///   is installed, or AName already is), ENOENT (no loaded module defines
///   AName), EACCES (a slot could not be written: every slot written is put
///   back), ENOMEM
/// @example `if HookInstall(GGetenv, "getenv", cpp("reinterpret_cast<void*>(&MyGetenv)")) then ... end;`
/// @see HookUninstall
/// @since 0.2
exported routine HookInstall(var AHook: Hook; const AName: ptr to const char; const AReplacement: ptr): bool;
begin
  return HookDoInstallName(AName, AReplacement, AHook.Original, AHook.State);
end;

/// Uninstalls a run-time hook: every slot it wrote whose module is still
/// loaded gets back exactly what it held before; nothing else is written.
/// AHook.State becomes nil; AHook.Original stays.
/// @param AHook a record HookInstall filled
/// @returns true when uninstalled; false with errno: EINVAL (AHook is not
///   installed), EACCES (a slot could not be written back: the hook stays
///   installed, the slots that went back stay back), ENOMEM
/// @example `HookUninstall(GGetenv);`
/// @see HookInstall
/// @since 0.2
exported routine HookUninstall(var AHook: Hook): bool;
begin
  return HookDoUninstallState(AHook.State);
end;

end.
